 On this baseline, ocean loading contributes appreciably. We compute the solid-Earth tide following the IERS conventions^16^ and the loading potential from FES2022,^17,18^ including water attraction, induced Earth potential and clock displacement.^19^ For the principal lunar semidiurnal tide, M₂, the differential solid-tide and loading amplitudes are $3.41\times10^{-18}$ and $1.42\times10^{-18}$ in fractional frequency, and their 20° phase difference gives a combined amplitude of $4.76\times10^{-18}$ (Fig. 1c).
 
-The record comprises 544 h of retained data in five campaigns and 54 observing segments over 353 days (Fig. 1b). We analyse it in two reductions, both with segment offsets. The primary reduction uses the data after transient screening and applies a 1,200-s triangular filter at 600-s steps to observations and model alike. The auxiliary reduction consists of 3,299 non-overlapping 600-s means from the same 54 segments, with 545.9 h of retained samples, and is used without the triangular filter. Their selections, weights and template realizations differ (Methods). The auxiliary reduction provides the summary responses, spectra and signal-to-noise ratios, and the primary reduction provides the time-domain displays and robustness tests (Supplementary Methods SM6).
