+Sustained network operation would extend phase coverage, and better clock stability would increase sensitivity for a given observing time. Continuous runs of at least two days with maintained phase lock cover successive diurnal cycles, a longer calendar span separates neighbouring frequencies, and gaps create sidelobes (Supplementary Fig. 2). Together with additional sites and local environmental records, improved coverage and stability would allow weaker potential changes to be identified after subtraction of the tidal background.
 
